{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.NonsingularInverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension.activeSetCard_le_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension.activeSetCard_le_pred","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LPActiveSetDimension.lean#L116-L121","doc":"The same bound in the `≤ d - 1` form the probe reports. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension.activeSetCard_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension.activeSetCard_lt","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LPActiveSetDimension.lean#L99-L114","doc":"**The LP's active set is bounded by the size of the operator basis.**\n\n`hcs` is complementary slackness on the optimal primal-dual pair: a non-zero\ndual multiplier forces its Frobenius constraint tight.  The conclusion mentions\nneither the cost vector `t`, nor `n_target` beyond its non-vanishing, nor any\nproperty of `G` beyond invertibility — in particular not its sparsity.  So\npassing from an orthogonal basis to a non-orthogonal one cannot raise this\nbound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension.tightSetCard_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension.tightSetCard_lt","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LPActiveSetDimension.lean#L86-L97","doc":"**The tight set is a proper subset of the index set**, hence has cardinality\n`< d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension.exists_slack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.LPActiveSetDimension.exists_slack","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LPActiveSetDimension.lean#L67-L84","doc":"**Not every Frobenius constraint can be tight.**  If the Gram `G` is\ninvertible and the net constraint `∑ i, x i = n` is non-zero, some coordinate of\n`G.mulVec x` is non-zero.\n\nThis is the whole content: `G x = 0` forces `x = 0` by injectivity, and then the\nnet constraint reads `0 = n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}